;; target-countries.edn — the denominator for the breadth axis.
;;
;; Countries with a functioning LEI-issuing registry and an economy large
;; enough that a worldwide corporate catalog omitting them is visibly
;; incomplete. Written out explicitly, and kept in the loop repo rather than
;; inside the scoring library, because it is a JUDGEMENT about ambition, not a
;; fact about scoring -- someone should be able to disagree with this list and
;; change it without touching the rubric.
;;
;; An implicit "every country on earth" denominator was rejected: no catalog
;; reaches ~195 countries, so breadth would sit permanently near zero and stop
;; carrying information about whether the catalog is improving.

["AE" "AR" "AT" "AU" "BE" "BR" "CA" "CH" "CL" "CN" "CO" "CZ" "DE" "DK" "EG" "ES" "ET" "FI" "FR" "GB" "GH" "GR" "HK" "HU" "ID" "IE" "IL" "IN" "IT" "JP" "KE" "KR" "KW" "LU" "MA" "MX" "MY" "NG" "NL" "NO" "NZ" "PE" "PH" "PK" "PL" "PT" "QA" "RO" "SA" "SE" "SG" "TH" "TR" "TW" "UA" "US" "VN" "ZA"]
